  "title": "Intracranial recordings before and after left anterior temporal lobe disconnection during a speech prediction task (Kocsis et al., 2023) - derivative",
  "description": "Acute intracranial (electrocorticography) recordings from two epilepsy surgery patients at the University of Iowa, collected during a speech prediction task minutes before and after neurosurgical disconnection of the left anterior temporal lobe (a semantic hub). Recordings cover frontal grids, temporal pole, subtemporal and lateral temporal strips, and a Heschl's gyrus depth electrode. This derivative release provides data downsampled to 1000 Hz and a denoised version (demodulated band transform plus removal of the first SVD component), in BIDS format.",
  "methods_description": "ECoG was sampled at 2000 Hz (TDT, 0.7-800 Hz) and downsampled to 1000 Hz. Denoised versions were produced with demodulated band transform denoising and removal of the first SVD component. Recordings were made at least 20 minutes after anaesthesia stopped, before and after left ATL disconnection, during a speech prediction task with biasing sentences and target words. Data were repackaged as BrainVision float32 files with events and electrode tables.",
